B.ZI=new A.y(B.a26,["SSD stands for Seven-Segment Display! It gets its name from the 7 rectangular LED segments arranged in a figure-8 pattern.","All seven segments! Segments A, B, C, D, E, F, and G all turn ON together to display the full number 8.","In Common Cathode, all 7 LEDs share one negative GND pin; sending HIGH (5V) turns a segment ON. In Common Anode, they share +5V; sending LOW (0V) turns a segment ON.","Using a BCD-to-7-segment decoder chip (like the CD4511)! It takes a 4-bit binary code (0000 to 1001 for numbers 0-9) and decodes it to light the correct segments."],t.w)
B.YK=new A.y(B.ae,["SSD (Seven-Segment Display)","How does a 7-Segment Display (SSD) combine 7 LEDs to display numbers 0 to 9?","A 7-Segment Display (SSD) packs 7 individual rectangular LED bars arranged in a figure-8 layout (labeled A, B, C, D, E, F, G) plus a decimal point (DP). By turning specific segment LEDs ON, any digit from 0 to 9 can be clearly displayed (e.g. Segments B+C = 1, A+B+G+E+D = 2, all 7 = 8)!","Real-Life Memory Analogy: Like a digital stadium scoreboard or an elevator floor indicator! Instead of drawing whole numbers with chalk, you just light up the right neon bars to form any crisp digital number.","Cause & Effect: Why use an SSD instead of separate LEDs? An SSD provides an instant human-readable numeric readout (speed, countdown seconds, distance in cm) in one compact package without needing a bulky LCD or computer screen!","Real-World Everyday Places: Digital alarm clocks (07:30), microwave countdown timers, elevator floor screens, petrol pump meters, and digital multimeters.","When to Use It: Whenever your robot needs to display live scores, countdown timers, measured distance in cm, or robot battery percentage.",B.Ug,B.Vv,B.ZI],t.R)
